<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-16-black-and-white.png" alt="https://archive.org/details/batsfordchesspuz0000bard/page/151/mode/1up" width="382" height="387" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-73520" srcset="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-16-black-and-white.png 382w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-06-16-black-and-white-300x304.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 382px) 100vw, 382px" /></p>
<p>A puzzle in chess logic from <a href="https://archive.org/details/batsfordchesspuz0000bard/page/151/mode/1up"><em>The Batsford Chess Puzzle Book</em></a>. Who made the last move, and what was it? (There&#8217;s no trick &#8212; everything is just as it seems.)</p>

